/*****************************************************************************
    jitJ4 -- RUNG 4 OF THE jitLadder. 2026-07-31.   J3 + do.

    THE CLAIM THIS RUNG ADDS: the body runs ONCE EVEN WHEN THE CONDITION STARTS
    FALSE. That is the do/while contract and it is the ONLY thing distinguishing
    `do` from `while` -- so a rung that did not test it would be re-testing J3.

        do jdIn = jdIn - 2; while jdIn > 0;

        fire 1   jdIn = 10  ->   0   (5 iterations, same as a while would give)
        fire 2   jdIn = 0   ->  -2   (condition FALSE at entry; body ran ONCE)

    ⚠ FIRE 2 IS THE RUNG. Its value is diagnostic on its own, per rung style:
         -2   correct -- do semantics, body ran once
          0   WHILE SEMANTICS -- the body was skipped, the branch was not moved
         -4   the body ran twice on a condition that was false at entry

    Fire 1 is the regression net: it proves the loop still iterates properly and
    that moving the branch did not break the ordinary case.

    THE TOPOLOGY DIFFERENCE, which is one branch target:
        while:  entry -> cond -> (body -> cond)*      condition FIRST
        do:     entry -> body -> cond -> (body ...)   BODY FIRST

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (standing harness rule H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder4);
define
    jdIn;
    jitJ4 code={
        do jdIn = jdIn - 2;
        while jdIn > 0;
        };
    ;

jdIn = 10;
print "J4 fire 1 setup : jdIn =" jdIn:;
testing(jitJ4);
print "J4 fire 1 result: jdIn =" jdIn " (want 0)":;

/*  ⚠ NO RECOMPILE. And the input is chosen so the CONDITION IS FALSE AT ENTRY.  */
jdIn = 0;
print "J4 fire 2 setup : jdIn =" jdIn " (condition false at entry; recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "J4 fire 2 result: jdIn =" jdIn " (want -2; 0 = body SKIPPED = while semantics)":;

/*  ⚠ ORACLE LAST -- calling the action interpreted first consumes its isCoded
    state and testing() silently routes to jitRunIfTest.  */
jdIn = 10;
jitJ4();
print "J4 interpreted  : jdIn =" jdIn " (the oracle -- want 0)":;

print "J4 SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
